==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*loodak}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*loŋe-||to throw, push away}}. Probably related to {{cog|myv|лиемс||to prepare yarn for weaving}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation|*}}

===Verb===
{{fi-verb}}

# {{lb|fi|transitive}} to [[create]] {{gloss|bring into existence; make, produce}}
#* {{quote-book|fi|year=1933/1938|title={{w|fi:Pyhä Raamattu|Raamattu}}|trans-title=The Bible|publisher={{w|lang=fi|Suomen Pipliaseura}}|location=Helsinki|chapter=1. Mooseksen kirja 1:1|trans-chapter={{w|Book of Genesis}} 1:1|passage=Alussa '''loi''' Jumala taivaan ja maan.|translation=In the beginning God '''created''' the heaven and the earth.}}
# {{lb|fi|transitive}} to [[shovel]] {{gloss|move with a shovel}}
#: {{coi|fi|'''luoda''' lunta|to '''shovel''' snow}}
# {{lb|fi|partitive verb}} to [[shed]] {{gloss|radiate, cast, give off light}}
#: {{coi|fi|'''luoda''' katseensa|to '''set''' eyes on|q=+ illative}}
#: {{ux|fi|Lamppu '''luo''' sinistä valoa.|The lamp '''sheds''' blue light.}}
# {{lb|fi|transitive|always with an object}} to [[moult]]/[[molt]], [[exuviate]], [[slough]] {{gloss|to shed or cast off a covering, especially a skin}}
#: {{ux|fi|Käärme alkoi '''luoda nahkaansa'''.|The snake began to '''moult'''.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Kun hummeri kasvaa, se '''luo kuorensa'''.|As it grows, a lobster will '''exuviate'''.}}
# {{lb|fi|weaving|transitive}} to [[warp]] {{gloss|arrange so that they run lengthwise in weaving}}
# {{lb|fi|archaic|transitive}} to [[begin]], [[start]]<ref>Kolehmainen, T. 2001. ”Loihesi lausumahan”. Kieli-ikkuna. Helsingin Sanomat 14.8.2001. https://www.kotus.fi/nyt/kolumnit_artikkelit_ja_esitelmat/kieli-ikkuna_(1996_2010)/loihesi_lausumahan</ref>

